# Chakravyuh admin dashboard — example snippet for Caddy (reverse proxy + TLS).
#
# Exposes the dashboard (port 5000 of the chakravyuh-ai container) on its own TLS subdomain,
# SEPARATE from the public honeypot and from the sensor subdomain. The gate is the Chakravyuh
# login (cookie session); Caddy only acts as reverse proxy + TLS.
#
# Requirements:
#   1) DNS:  A  chakravyuh-admin.example.com  ->  <your server's IP>
#   2) chakravyuh-ai reachable from your Caddy (same Docker network) and listening on :5000
#      (add your proxy's external network to the `chakravyuh` service — see docker-compose.vps.yml).
#   3) In the compose file: CHAKRAVYUH_COOKIE_SECURE=true and an admin password set
#      (or read ONCE from the container log).
#
# Add this block to your Caddyfile and reload Caddy. Adjust the domain and, if your Caddy runs
# in a container, the service name (chakravyuh-ai) to match your network.

chakravyuh-admin.example.com {
	encode gzip zstd
	reverse_proxy chakravyuh-ai:5000
}
